HOME_FAQS = [
 ('How much does decking cost in Cornwall?', 'Every deck is different. The price depends on size, height, ground conditions, the boards you choose and any balustrading or steps. We offer a free site survey and a fixed, itemised quote so you know exactly what you are paying for.'),
 ('Composite or hardwood decking: which is better for Cornwall?', 'Composite decking is very low maintenance, will not rot and copes well with salty coastal air. Hardwood gives a natural look and ages beautifully with care. We talk you through the pros, cons and costs for your site.'),
 ('Do I need planning permission for decking in Cornwall?', 'Most ground-level garden decks do not, but decks more than 30cm above ground, decks at listed buildings and some decks in conservation areas may. We will flag anything that needs checking with Cornwall Council before work begins.'),
 ('How long does it take to install a deck?', 'A typical garden deck takes a few days to a week. Larger, raised or multi-level decks with glass balustrades take longer. We give you a clear timeline with your quote.'),
 ('Do you repair existing decks?', 'Yes. We replace damaged boards and joists, fix loose or unsafe railings, and clean, sand and re-oil tired timber. If a repair is not worthwhile we will tell you honestly.'),
 ('Can you supply decking materials only?', 'Yes. We supply decking boards, framing, fixings, lighting and balustrade kits for DIY and trade customers across Cornwall.'),
 ('Which areas of Cornwall do you cover?', 'We cover the whole of Cornwall, from Bude and Launceston to Penzance and the Lizard. If you are searching for decking near me anywhere in Cornwall, get in touch with your postcode.'),
]
